# Everything the image does not need. Each line here is build context that is
# otherwise uploaded to the daemon on every build, and — worse — a file that
# could end up in a layer.

# The database and uploaded audio. These belong to the machine that made them:
# baking a development database into an image ships its accounts with it.
data/

# 571 MB of history, none of which runs.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules/

# Acceptance screenshots are generated by the test harness and no longer
# tracked at all; the pattern stays so a local run cannot leak 27 MB into a
# build context.
docs/

# The test harness and the developer tooling. None of it runs in production,
# and Playwright in particular would drag a browser in.
#
# NOT excluded, though they look like they should be: src/ and
# tailwind.config.js. The build stage compiles the stylesheet and needs both.
# Excluding them here makes `docker build` fail on the COPY, which is at least
# a loud failure — but the reason is worth writing down rather than
# rediscovering.
scripts/
cai-dat/

# Windows-only helper config, which may hold an administrator password.
cai-dat/cau-hinh.bat

# Anything holding a real credential must never be part of a build context.
.env
.env.*
*.local

npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
